#turn undead spoiler
**** **** **** **** **** **** **** **** **** **** **** **** **** ****
turn-343.txt
Priest(ess) and Knights using #turn in NetHack 3.4.3
Compiled by cdi <cdinchauste@hotmail.com>

I couldn't find a good spoiler describing just how the #turn undead
ability worked, so I thought I'd write one.  Comments and corrections
are welcome.
**** **** **** **** **** **** **** **** **** **** **** **** **** ****

This spoiler only covers a Knight or Priest(ess) using the #turn
extended command.  Other classes using #turn will attempt to cast the
spell "turn undead" or be told "You don't know how to turn undead!"

If you are a Knight or Priest(ess), attempting to #turn will fail
under any of the following circumstances:

1) You are non-chaotic and polymorphed into a demon or undead creature.
2) u.ugangr > 6 /* "Die, mortal!" */ [2]
   "For some reason, <god> seems to ignore you."
        - you aggravate monsters
        - you abuse your wisdom

3) You are in hell.
   "Since you are in Gehennom, <god> won't help you."
        - you aggravate monsters

4) You are confused.
   "Unfortunately, your voice falters."
        - all non-peaceful undead (and demons, if you are XL:15
          or greater) within range are unscared, unfrozen, and
          woken up. [3]

Otherwise, you turn all the hostile undead (and demons, if you are
XL:15 or greater) within range that fail to resist [1].  For a monster
to be affected it must be within line-of-sight and within a radius of
5 plus your XL/5 (rounded down) from your position.

If you are sufficiently experienced and an undead creature fails to
resist twice, it will be destroyed (if you are lawful/neutral) or
pacified (if you are chaotic). Table 1 indicates at which level the
various undead monster types are eligible for being destroyed or
pacified by #turning.  Table 2 indicates the probability that a
successful #turning will destroy or pacify the creature, if you are
the minimum XL required for that monster type.

Successfully #turning or attempting to #turn while confused will
leave you frozen and vunerable for five turns.  Take precautions to
protect yourself during this time.

